      "values": [
        "https://arxiv.org/abs/2004.12497v11",
        "",
        "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.987654321",
        "The outer center-pedal area product in elliptic billiards \u2014 Alec Kriebel, v1.0,2026-10-16. AMR-050-0015 /5100015 /k303,b. Signed product of outer tangent-polygon area and actual perpendicular-center-foot area on its boundary tangent side LINES; strict nondegenerate confocal elliptical caustic, periods not divisible by four, admitted coprime stars, reversal and fixed repeats(d\u00b2); circle separate. Explicit fixed-linear edge-vector map and classical odd cyclic Jacobi identity give a full all-phase proof and constant. KLS2002, KS2003/2004, AST/BT2020, Stachel/Jacobi/conic and established pole methods credited. A.Ferudun2026v1.1 Theorem2/Section6 DOI10.5281/zenodo.23088516 is the exact full contemporary theorem; v1.0 centered primitive even subset distinguished. Historical ordering, independent non-derivation and novelty undetermined; no first-proof/exclusive/new-identity/current-worldwide-open claim. Required fresh sequential whole-package reviews/global fixes completed before deposit; portable eight-suite exact/uncertified numerical controls, originals and correction evidence retained. Extensive AI use; unrefereed, no independent human peer review/formal proof verification. PR:https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/pull/209"
      ],
